# `codegen`

`Bake` orchestrates proto output plus per-integration generation from `schema` DTOs.

Consume schema's resolved envelope variants, entity wire fields, scalar/collection metadata and catalog item/key metadata; do not allocate tags or repeat type/key lookup. Legacy DTO adaptation belongs at generation boundaries. `codec_metadata.go` contains backend input adapters, not YAML policy or a universal message IR. Language-specific reader/writer mappings, omit-zero guards, public shapes and operation availability stay in codegen.

`go_payload.go`, `js_payload.go` and `cs_payload.go` each share ordinary command/event emission. `envelope_codecs.go` has one emitter per language over ordered variants. Go retains encode/decode for all envelopes; JS/C# command envelopes encode only, other envelopes decode only. Preserve Go's last recognized oneof versus JS/C#'s separate properties. `scalar_encode.go` shares JS/C# scalar guards between ordinary/custom messages; Go retains its own scalar helper. Go entity and world collection emission share element/map-entry algorithms with explicit ordinary/delta presence; nil/undefined/null means absent and a present empty delta collection means clear.

`goFullStateProjection` plus the `fullStateLiteral` template share authoritative/public state construction at generation time. Preserve the wrappers' locks, revision capture, shallow collection references, owner-only tick/once redaction and serialization after unlocking. Keep compact serialization and dirty-mask deltas separate; add no generated runtime identifiers for this helper.

Compatibility evidence lives in the resolution baseline, characterization and generated-consumer tests. Freeze supported wire bytes, public APIs and fingerprint preimages; retain known string/bytes-list framing differences, empty-custom-element behavior, Go unknown map-entry behavior, C# scalar-map default inference and Go tick-bytes limitations until separately reviewed corrections. `GOLEM_REQUIRE_CONSUMERS=1` makes missing compiler/runtime prerequisites fail rather than skip; `GOLEM_CONSUMER_RACE=1` runs generated Go consumers with the race detector.

`RemoveIntegration` only supports shared-only targets without extra emitters or finalizers. It preflights known output names, regular files, the generated header and resolved project containment before removing those files. It must never recursively delete an output directory or alter consumer configuration.

Templates live under `codegen/templates/` and are embedded with `go:embed`.

`integration_outputs.go` owns integration defaults, output names/roles, optional selection and historical JS intermediate recognition. Successful JS finalization removes only top-level regular recognized intermediates bearing the Golem generated header; preserve declarations, unmarked files, unreadable files and nonregular entries. The temporary compiler config is handled separately. `integration.go` preserves the public compatibility projection. Keep descriptors read-only and decorate per-integration entity DTO copies. The relative containment predicate is shared; bridge removal resolves symlinks and rejects Rel failures, while Threlte validation remains lexical with its existing error policy.

`go_proto.go`, `js_proto.go`, and `csharp_proto.go` generate lightweight codecs for consumers. Optional checked protocol constant sets are emitted in the existing entities outputs as Go untyped constants, TypeScript `as const` objects/unions, and C# static string classes; they are not protobuf fields and do not alter `entities.proto`. Keep Go, JS, and C# client targets conceptually parallel.

**Go server entities (`templates/go_server/server.go.tmpl`):** each `Synced*` carries a runtime-only unexported `srv *golem.Server` plus exported `BindServer` / `Server()` (not wire/snapshot state). `Server()` may be nil before `CreateEntity`; wrapper types embedding `*Synced*` inherit both methods. When `EntityData.Collider` is set, emit `Collider()` (2D) or `Collider3D()` (3D) from schema shape/layer/trigger; wrappers inherit and may override intentionally. When `HasOwnerVars`, emit `OwnerScopedEntity` (`PublicFullUpdate` omitting owner-only tick/once fields, `PublicReplicationMask` clearing owner-only tick bits via `*OwnerOnlyMask`); keep authoritative `FullState`/`FullUpdate` unchanged for persistence and owner delivery. Do not emit those methods for entities without owner-only vars.

**Go server shared (`templates/go_server/shared.go.tmpl`):** when `SharedData.Collision` is set, `Runtime` includes `Layers`+`EnableCollision` (2D) or `Layers3D`+`EnableCollision3D` (3D) that call `MustCollisionBackend`/`MustCollisionBackend3D` (nil panics before any Server setter), build the YAML named matrix, bind the backend, and call `SetCollisionBackend`/`SetCollisionLayers` (or 3D equivalents). Omit those fields/methods when there is no collision config so projects without collision still compile. Always emit `Runtime.LoadSnapshotIfExists` and blocking `Runtime.RunSnapshotAutosave` (plus unexported `startSnapshotAutosave` / `runSnapshotAutosave` for injectable ticker/ticks/save in tests; validate ctx/interval before ticker creation; check `ctx.Err` before each save); keep `context`/`errors`/`os`/`time` imports valid with or without entities/commands/events/world/collision. Do not add these helpers to non-Go-server client templates.

`codegen/` imports config and template data from `schema`; it should not define YAML schema structs or reimplement schema loading.

When adding an integration, register its output specification in `integration_outputs.go` and add its templates and any `GenerateExtra` or `Finalize` hooks here. Integrations may be shared-only by omitting `Template`/`FileNamer` and emitting only `SharedTemplates`. Full clients (`go-client`, `js-client`, `csharp-client`) own generated managers/codecs; engine integrations (`phaser`, `threlte`, `unity`, `ebiten`) should stay thin and depend on the matching full client output.

`threlte` emits only `GolemThrelte.ts`, with typed manager adapters, reactive bindings, component props and complete component/headless registrations. It reuses generated JS entities/world/events/commands and never generates Svelte components, codecs, or presentation choices. The application's Svelte toolchain compiles this bridge; there is no integration finalizer. `threlte_config.go` validates its JS dependency and separate output before generation. Shared-only removal applies unchanged.
